menu "Task Diagnostics"

config KFEAT_SNAPSHOT
    bool "Task snapshot support"
    default y if BUILD_TYPE_DEBUG
    help
      Enable reusable task/CPU snapshot collection and backtrace dumping
      support in `ktask::snapshot`. Debug builds enable this by default so
      panic, watchdog, and manual diagnostic paths can collect task state.

config KFEAT_SYSRQ
    bool "SysRq task snapshot trigger"
    depends on KFEAT_SNAPSHOT
    default y if BUILD_TYPE_DEBUG
    help
      Expose `/proc/sysrq-trigger` and route supported SysRq commands to the
      shared snapshot service. Debug builds enable this by default; release
      builds can still opt in when operator-triggered diagnostics are needed.

config KFEAT_WATCHDOG
    bool "Watchdog diagnostics"
    depends on KFEAT_SNAPSHOT
    help
      Enable watchdog-driven diagnostic checks such as soft lockup detection
      and lock-wait heuristics.

config KFEAT_SCHED_STAT
    bool "Scheduler statistics"
    default y if BUILD_TYPE_DEBUG
    help
      Enable low-overhead per-CPU scheduler counters for diagnostics. The
      counters are exposed through `/proc/sched_stat`; the watchdog also
      prints them when reporting a soft lockup. Debug builds enable this by
      default, while release builds keep it opt-in.

config KFEAT_WATCHDOG_HARDLOCKUP
    bool "Watchdog hard lockup detection"
    depends on KFEAT_WATCHDOG
    depends on MACHINE_AARCH64_QEMU
    depends on KFEAT_NMI
    help
      Enable the hard lockup watchdog backend. Requires NMI support (the
      source is selected together with NMI).  On AArch64 QEMU virt this is
      currently implemented through the PMU-backed periodic NMI source and
      global snapshot rendezvous.

config KFEAT_LOCK_STAT
    bool "Lock contention statistics (/proc/lock_stat)"
    default y if BUILD_TYPE_DEBUG
    help
      Enable per-class lock contention statistics for kernel mutexes, rwlocks,
      and spinlocks. Statistics are exposed through `/proc/lock_stat`. Debug
      builds enable this by default, while release builds keep it opt-in
      because lock-path instrumentation has runtime cost.

endmenu
